href%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fwww.businessinsider.com%2Ffamily-meetings-saved-marriage-after-becoming-mom%5C%22%20target%3D%5C%22_blank%5C%22%3Eweekly%20check-in%20ritual%3C%2Fa%3E.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EWe%20treat%20it%20like%20a%20physical%20for%20our%20relationship%3A%20It's%20a%20chance%20to%20celebrate%20what's%20working%2C%20catch%20small%20issues%20before%20they%20snowball%2C%20and%20make%20sure%20neither%20of%20us%20is%20quietly%20carrying%20resentment.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3ESo%20far%2C%20it's%20been%20the%20single%20%3Ca%20href%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fwww.businessinsider.com%2Fsigns-mature-relationship-improving-health-2024-2%5C%22%20target%3D%5C%22_blank%5C%22%3Emost%20helpful%20habit%3C%2Fa%3E%20we've%20adopted%20as%20a%20couple.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Ch2%20data-toc-id%3D%5C%221c5baa65-146b-4615-9014-780543799431%5C%22%3EWe%20use%20the%20same%20questions%20every%20week%3C%2Fh2%3E%3Cp%3EHaving%20a%20structured%20format%20works%20well%20for%20us.%20Instead%20of%20wasting%20time%20%E2%80%94%20%26quot%3BWhat%20do%20you%20want%20to%20talk%20about%3F%26quot%3B%20%26quot%3BI%20don't%20know%2C%20what%20do%20%3Cem%3Eyou%20%3C%2Fem%3Ewant%20to%20talk%20about%3F%26quot%3B%20%E2%80%94%20we%20just%20run%20down%20our%20list%2C%20each%20taking%20turns%20to%20talk%20or%20listen.%20While%20it%20took%20some%20trial-and-error%20to%20find%20the%20questions%20that%20are%20most%20beneficial%2C%20here's%20the%20set%20we%20landed%20on%3A%3C%2Fp%3E%3Col%3E%3Cli%3EWhat%20made%20you%20feel%20loved%20this%20week%3F%3C%2Fli%3E%3Cli%3EWhat's%20your%20biggest%20stressor%20looking%20ahead%20to%20next%20week%3F%20And%20what's%20one%20thing%20I%20can%20do%20to%20support%20you%3F%3C%2Fli%3E%3Cli%3EWhat's%20one%20thing%20you're%20really%20looking%20forward%20to%20this%20week%3F%3C%2Fli%3E%3Cli%3EWhat%20would%20make%20you%20feel%20connected%20to%20me%20this%20week%3F%3C%2Fli%3E%3Cli%3EIs%20there%20anything%20we%20should%20talk%20about%20now%20before%20it%20becomes%20a%20bigger%20issue%3F%3C%2Fli%3E%3C%2Fol%3E%3Cp%3EEach%20question%20serves%20a%20different%20purpose.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cfigure%3E%3Cimg%20width%3D%5C%223672%5C%22%20alt%3D%5C%22the%20author%20and%20her%20husband%20walking%20on%20a%20beach%5C%22%20src%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fi.insider.com%2F6aa1acecec15fe2d3cf156b9%3Fformat%3Djpeg%5C%22%20height%3D%5C%222976%5C%22%3E%3Cfigcaption%3EAsking%20the%20same%20questions%20each%20week%20helps%20keep%20them%20on%20track.%3Cp%3ECourtesy%20of%20Rebecca%20Strong%3C%2Fp%3E%3C%2Ffigcaption%3E%3C%2Ffigure%3E%3Ch2%20data-toc-id%3D%5C%22ba29b7cb-50aa-41ee-ad6e-af57a5d686b7%5C%22%3EThe%20first%20question%20encourages%20us%20to%20acknowledge%20each%20other's%20efforts%3C%2Fh2%3E%3Cp%3EDuring%20a%20busy%2C%20stressful%20week%2C%20it%20can%20be%20easy%20to%20overlook%20the%20little%20things%20we%20both%20do%20to%20care%20for%20each%20other.%20But%20my%20husband%20and%20I%20made%20a%20vow%20never%20to%20take%20each%20other%20for%20granted.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EThe%20first%20question%20%E2%80%94%20%26quot%3BWhat%20made%20you%20feel%20loved%20this%20week%3F%26quot%3B%20%E2%80%94%20offers%20a%20natural%20opportunity%20for%20us%20to%20%3Ca%20href%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fwww.businessinsider.com%2Fwhen-you-should-write-thank-you-notes-from-etiquette-experts%5C%22%20target%3D%5C%22_blank%5C%22%3Eexpress%20some%20gratitude%3C%2Fa%3E.%20I%20might%20let%20my%20husband%20know%20how%20much%20it%20meant%20to%20me%20that%20he%20got%20up%20with%20the%20baby%20in%20the%20middle%20of%20the%20night.%20He%20might%20thank%20me%20for%20making%20his%20morning%20easier%20by%20filling%20up%20his%20water%20bottle%20and%20watching%20our%20son%20while%20he%20worked%20out.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Ch2%20data-toc-id%3D%5C%22cf8cda06-4a1e-43c1-9063-2991aa3cefa9%5C%22%3EThen%2C%20we%20do%20some%20collaborative%20troubleshooting%3C%2Fh2%3E%3Cp%3EI%20find%20that%20naming%20my%20stressors%20out%20loud%20can%20help%20prevent%20me%20from%20spiraling%20inside%20my%20own%20head.%20Plus%2C%20when%20my%20husband%20and%20I%20share%20them%20with%20each%20other%2C%20we're%20able%20to%20proactively%20problem-solve%20together.%20Better%20yet%2C%20we%20both%20have%20the%20chance%20to%20explain%20exactly%20how%20we'd%20like%20to%20receive%20support%20from%20each%20other%20%E2%80%94%20rather%20than%20leaving%20each%20other%20to%20guess.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3ESo%2C%20if%20I%20tell%20him%20I'm%20%3Ca%20href%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fwww.businessinsider.com%2Fwhat-to-do-in-the-15-minutes-before-job-interview-2014-3%5C%22%20target%3D%5C%22_blank%5C%22%3Enervous%20about%20an%20interview%3C%2Fa%3E%20coming%20up%20this%20week%2C%20he%20could%20offer%20some%20confidence-boosting%20affirmation%2C%20and%20then%20I%20could%20ask%20him%20to%20rehearse%20my%20questions%20with%20me%20the%20night%20before%20so%20I%20feel%20prepared.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Ch2%20data-toc-id%3D%5C%22a0577c21-4adf-4ca2-be43-23d1d7d1ec05%5C%22%3EWe%20also%20balance%20things%20out%20with%20positive%20anticipation%3C%2Fh2%3E%3Cp%3EDuring%20our%20check-in%2C%20we're%20careful%20not%20to%20dwell%20too%20much%20on%20the%20potentially%20anxiety-inducing%20events%20coming%20up.%20Taking%20a%20moment%20to%20talk%20about%20the%20things%20we're%20looking%20forward%20to%2C%20whether%20it's%20a%20family%20walk%20or%20a%20special%20%3Ca%20href%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fwww.businessinsider.com%2Feasy-dinners-under-30-minutes-meal-planning-recipes-2025-3%5C%22%20target%3D%5C%22_blank%5C%22%3Ehome-cooked%20dinner%3C%2Fa%3E%2C%20helps%20us%20to%20feel%20excited%20about%20the%20week%20ahead.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Ch2%20data-toc-id%3D%5C%2214e33a3c-287d-4b5c-b53c-783901ec1e1a%5C%22%3EWe%20benefit%20from%20having%20an%20opportunity%20to%20express%20our%20needs%3C%2Fh2%3E%3Cp%3EMy%20husband%20and%20I%20have%20similar%20%3Ca%20href%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fwww.businessinsider.com%2Fshow-love-acts-of-service-love-language-nearly-ruined-marriage-2025-4%5C%22%20target%3D%5C%22_blank%5C%22%3Elove%20languages%3C%2Fa%3E%2C%20but%20we're%20not%20mind%20readers.%20We%20can't%20expect%20the%20other%20person%20to%20know%20exactly%20what%20we%20need%20from%20each%20other.%20That's%20precisely%20why%20we%20started%20asking%3A%20%26quot%3BWhat%20would%20make%20you%20feel%20connected%20to%20me%20this%20week%3F%26quot%3B%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3ESometimes%2C%20for%20me%2C%20it's%20often%20as%20simple%20as%20having%20breakfast%20together%20or%20getting%20a%20text%20check-in%20after%20my%20therapy%20appointment.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EFor%20him%2C%20it%20might%20just%20be%20an%20unprompted%20hug%20or%20putting%20our%20phones%20away%20while%20we%20watch%20something%20together.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cfigure%3E%3Cimg%20width%3D%5C%224032%5C%22%20alt%3D%5C%22the%20author%20and%20her%20husband%20sitting%20outside%20on%20a%20boardwalk%5C%22%20src%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fi.insider.com%2F6aa1ad3acc23a829a3b8f875%3Fformat%3Djpeg%5C%22%20height%3D%5C%223024%5C%22%3E%3Cfigcaption%3EThey%20express%20their%20needs%20during%20their%20check-in.%3Cp%3ECourtesy%20of%20Rebecca%20Strong%3C%2Fp%3E%3C%2Ffigcaption%3E%3C%2Ffigure%3E%3Ch2%20data-toc-id%3D%5C%22c2b3f5b0-6612-4ca8-9db3-c088db6dcd20%5C%22%3EFinally%2C%20we%20tackle%20any%20issues%20before%20they%20escalate%3C%2Fh2%3E%3Cp%3EIf%20there's%20one%20thing%20we've%20learned%20over%20the%20last%20eight%20years%20of%20our%20relationship%2C%20it's%20that%20there's%20a%20right%20and%20wrong%20time%20to%20bring%20up%20things%20that%20are%20bothering%20you.%20Confronting%20the%20other%20person%20at%20the%20end%20of%20a%20draining%20workday%2C%20or%20in%20a%20moment%20when%20one%20or%20both%20of%20you%20are%20already%20emotionally%20activated%2C%20is%20unlikely%20to%20lead%20to%20a%20productive%20discussion.%20That's%20why%20we%20always%20end%20our%20weekly%20check-ins%20on%20this%20question%3A%20Is%20there%20anything%20we%20should%20talk%20about%20now%20before%20it%20becomes%20a%20bigger%20issue%3F%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EThis%20gives%20us%20both%20peace%20of%20mind%20that%20there's%20a%20designated%20time%20to%20air%20out%20any%20concerns%2C%20so%20we%20don't%20feel%20the%20need%20to%20tackle%20them%20when%